{"title":"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For any polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/e/1fe5d52410379411b2041f59ded55b98e7dedd94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x) = a_0 + a_1 x + \\cdots + a_k x^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"230\" height=\"20\" /> with integer coefficients, the number of coefficients which are odd is denoted by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/d/95d33b7b4feb5e94e1ceaab9070342d9d25d3d0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w(P)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" />.  For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/d/09d421cc13e7243f73abcc08af3efb0dd38aeaf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i = 0, 1, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/3/45380490a52bb5384d110d7b680d337d02de8425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_i (x) = (1+x)^i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"19\" />.  Prove that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/7/f5776f619f1709dddd0946754b3015d2599eeeb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i_1, i_2, \\ldots , i_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" /> are integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/f/70f149a3fa5a6e977ca36f925df7d3b8d8a358df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq i_1 &lt; i_2 &lt; \\cdots &lt; i_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"169\" height=\"15\" />, then\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/c/edc5dc71da096f9e7bba32042a1e1e683157f148.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w(Q_{i_1} + Q_{i_2} + \\cdots + Q_{i_n}) \\ge w(Q_{i_1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"273\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We first observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/9/e799129551841e498b47f85a3ab5e1f6bbd6c976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+x)^{2^m} \\equiv 1 + x^{2^m} \\pmod{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"229\" height=\"20\" />, so for any polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> of degree less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/9/f2949376cf9667bec6117d164f65945d8a2c049f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^m$\" width=\"20\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/4/7443276a33dc28661b7236b8358309356ec795c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w(P\\cdot Q_{2^m}) = 2w (P)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"161\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be the largest power of 2 that is less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53276c3de04e6128f82a344ed66da1da12a7825.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />.  We proceed by induction on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/84574de7797bc7b4e1fc52075f4d265ba60a8bce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, the problem is trivial.\n</p><p>Now assume that the problem holds for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dc6fab4c2fdb4e9046030fbfdcf6ea721b05602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />.  We now have two cases: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/f/1df9efb594dc02be1a57bae7dfe43feaa8e1f41d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i_1 \\ge k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/e/33e509c50eef84480393a3b1648b4b08cb262abb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i_1 &lt; k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>In the first case, we note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/6/4c6a7d4c54cf3674ddb04f4dd86de3772d70c364.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w \\left( \\sum_{j=1}^{n}Q_{i_j} \\right) = w \\left( (1+x)^k \\sum_{j=1}^{n}Q_{i_j - k} \\right) = 2 w \\left( \\sum_{j=1}^{n}Q_{i_j - k} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"454\" height=\"54\" />, which is greater than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/5/895310d8d929d3dc57e4cbf1e255aa9cecc8e834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w( Q_{i_1} )$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> by assumption.\n</p><p>In the second case, we use the division algorithm to note that\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/6/9362036057b5d05337e077d3705648d3c56d2c46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j=1}^{n}Q_{i_j} = \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}a_j x^j + (1+x)^k \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} b_j x^j \\equiv \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}\\left[ (a_j + b_j)x^j + b_j x^{j+k} \\right] \\pmod{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"590\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>But by assumption, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/c/f3c8d2abed966157edccee5faddb8c8abc277377.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w \\left( \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}a_j x^j \\right) \\ge w( Q_{i_1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"184\" height=\"54\" />, and for each odd <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/0785f19824c8b23ab3dfe000b471994078fdf589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" />, at least one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/f/11f5d7b8ca9a27ad42cd2e39cbc338d9bc95f4cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_j + b_j )$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfbbf3e10280b5771976f3342b10181e4b31d4fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"17\" /> must be odd, Q.E.D.\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO\" title=\"1985 IMO\">1985 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017175232\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.050 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 126/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1238/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4907/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.490      1 -total\n 55.04%    7.425      1 Template:IMO_box\n 43.63%    5.886      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4154:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017175232 and revision id 190820. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}